    "excerpt": "Coding ya typing ke beech chips khane se keyboard tel se bhar jata hai. Ye 5 dry roasted snacks jo laptop ko clean rakhein.",
    "content": "<p>Every professional working on a laptop knows the frustration of greasy fingertips, sticky trackpads, and crumb-covered keycaps. Traditional Indian tea snacks like samosas, kachoris, and butter biscuits leave oil films on tech hardware and deliver massive doses of refined maida that slow down cognitive processing.</p>\n<h2>Why Label Transparency Matters Here</h2>\n<p>Snacks advertised as 'baked' or 'roasted' often mask their true fat content. Manufacturers roast grains first, then spray them with hot fractionated palm oil to help synthetic flavor powders stick. Checking the fat percentage on the back panel reveals whether a snack is truly clean or just oil-coated under a baked label claim.</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>GudTree Golden Rule:</strong> If you need to wipe your fingers on a tissue paper after three bites, that snack does not belong near your work keyboard.</p></blockquote>\n<h2>Smart Daily Swaps for Clean Eating</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Stone-Ground Methi Khakhra:</strong> 100% whole wheat or multigrain dough roasted on an iron tawa with vacuum-sealed zero grease.</li>\n  <li><strong>Roasted Kala Chana:</strong> Crispy unpeeled chickpeas delivering 7g plant protein per handful with dry crunch.</li>\n  <li><strong>Puffed Jowar &amp; Bajra:</strong> Ancient millet pops roasted with black pepper and turmeric instead of cheese powders.</li>\n  <li><strong>Air-Popped Spiced Murmura:</strong> Kolkata-style dry roasted rice flakes tossed with unpolished peanuts and curry leaves.</li>\n  <li><strong>Dry Roasted Pumpkin Seeds:</strong> Natural sources of zinc and tryptophan to keep mental stress manageable.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Quick Nutrition Audit Summary</h2>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Desk Crunch Pick</th><th>Grease Level</th><th>Base Grain</th><th>Sugar Spike Risk</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>Bakery Butter Biscuits</td><td>Extreme (Refined Shortening)</td><td>Refined Wheat (Maida)</td><td>Very High (40% sugar)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Deep-Fried Namkeen Mix</td><td>High (Palmolein Film)</td><td>Gram Flour &amp; Maida</td><td>High (Rapid digestion)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>GudTree Methi Khakhra</td><td>Zero Grease (Bone Dry)</td><td>100% Whole Wheat &amp; Methi</td><td>Very Low (Slow carb release)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>GudTree Bhuna Chana</td><td>Zero Grease (Bone Dry)</td><td>Whole Black Gram</td><td>Extremely Low (GI &lt; 28)</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Stock your desk drawer with bone-dry whole food staples to protect both your computer hardware and your mid-afternoon productivity.</p>",
