    "readTime": "4 min read",
    "excerpt": "Packet par 'Baked Not Fried' padh kar khareed rahe hain? Peeth peeche 20% palm oil aur refined starches ka sach jaaniye.",
    "content": "<p>Walk down any Indian supermarket aisle or scroll Zepto's snack category, and you will see dozens of sleek pastel pouches boasting 'Baked, Never Fried', '60% Less Fat', and 'Heart Healthy'. Young professionals eagerly pay a 2x price premium for these packets, believing they are making an ultra-healthy choice.</p>\n<h2>Why Label Transparency Matters Here</h2>\n<p>Under FSSAI labeling guidelines, a manufacturer can truthfully claim a product is 'baked' as long as the dough passed through an oven conveyor. However, baking extruded starch leaves it completely dry and powdery. To make seasoning stick and ensure a crisp mouthfeel, factories spray the hot baked crisps with high-pressure atomized refined palmolein oil or hydrogenated fats before packaging.</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>GudTree Golden Rule:</strong> Always turn the packet around. If the second or third ingredient is 'Edible Vegetable Oil (Palmolein)', that snack contains up to 25% refined fat regardless of what the front slogan proclaims.</p></blockquote>\n<h2>Smart Daily Swaps for Clean Eating</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Read the Fat Per 100g:</strong> Truly clean dry snacks contain under 5g to 8g of total fat per 100g. If your 'baked' chip lists 20g–26g fat, it is heavily oil-sprayed.</li>\n  <li><strong>Check the Oil Source:</strong> Seek brands using cold-pressed groundnut, coconut, or olive oil instead of generic 'edible vegetable oil'.</li>\n  <li><strong>Upgrade to Home Puffed Millets:</strong> Dry roast ragi flakes, jowar puffs, or flat rice (poha) in a dry pan with mustard seeds and curry leaves.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Quick Nutrition Audit Summary</h2>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Product Type</th><th>Front-of-Pack Claim</th><th>Back-Panel Ingredient #2</th><th>Actual Fat by Weight</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>Market 'Diet' Crisp</td><td>\"Baked Not Fried - 50% Less Fat\"</td><td>Refined Palmolein Oil</td><td>22.5% Fat</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Traditional Fried Sev</td><td>\"Classic Indian Namkeen\"</td><td>Edible Vegetable Oil (Fried)</td><td>36.0% Fat</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>GudTree Dry Roasted Puffs</td><td>100% Air-Popped Millets</td><td>Whole Grain Sorghum (No oil spray)</td><td>3.8% Fat</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Scrutinizing ingredient lists instead of trusting front-panel marketing slogans ensures your hard-earned wellness budget actually supports clean cardiovascular health.</p>",
