    "excerpt": "Hostel room me na gas hai na fridge. Ye 5 dry snacks jo pocket-friendly hain aur padhai ke beech instant energy dete hain.",
    "content": "<p>College students and hostel residents preparing for competitive exams like JEE, NEET, UPSC, or CAT face a brutal nutrition dilemma: hostel mess food is uninspiring, cooking equipment is prohibited, and pocket allowances are modest. When late-night study hunger strikes, ultra-processed instant noodles and ₹10 chips become default choices.</p>\n<h2>Why Label Transparency Matters Here</h2>\n<p>Instant noodles cost ₹14 a packet, but provide empty calories from bleached white flour, industrial palm oil, and high sodium (over 800mg per serving). Eating them 4 nights a week causes persistent digestive sluggishness, dehydration, facial acne, and mental fatigue that directly damages academic retention.</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>GudTree Golden Rule:</strong> Traditional Indian dry grocery staples offer far superior nutritional density per rupee than any brightly packaged convenience snack.</p></blockquote>\n<h2>Smart Daily Swaps for Clean Eating</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Kirana Bhuna Chana (₹15 per 100g):</strong> 19g of complete plant protein, unpeeled fiber, and zinc that requires zero cooking or chilling.</li>\n  <li><strong>Unpolished Roasted Peanuts (₹12 per 50g):</strong> Nutrient-dense heart-healthy monounsaturated fats and natural biotin for student endurance.</li>\n  <li><strong>Puffed Rice Murmura Bhel (₹10 per bowl):</strong> Toss plain murmura with a pinch of rock salt, chopped onion, and lemon juice for an instant crunch.</li>\n  <li><strong>Desi Til-Gud Chikki (₹10 slab):</strong> Iron-rich natural jaggery and sesame seeds that eliminate evening sweet cravings cleanly.</li>\n  <li><strong>Dry Roasted Makhana (₹30 loose bag):</strong> Light, crunchy foxnuts to satisfy nervous chewing habits without calorie overload.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Quick Nutrition Audit Summary</h2>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Cost</th><th>Cooking Equipment Needed</th><th>Protein &amp; Fiber</th><th>Skin &amp; Energy Impact</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>Hostel Instant Cup Noodles</td><td>₹45</td><td>Kettle / Hot Water</td><td>2g Protein / 0.5g Fiber</td><td>Bloating, oil flare-ups, 2 AM crash</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Kirana Bhuna Chana + Peanuts</td><td>₹25</td><td>None (Ready to eat)</td><td>15g Protein / 7g Fiber</td><td>Clean sustained alertness, zero bloat</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Equipping your study table with dry glass jars of roasted chana, peanuts, and puffed grains keeps both your mind alert and your student budget intact.</p>",
