    "author": "GudTree Editorial Team",
    "authorRole": "Hormonal Nutrition Researchers",
    "authorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1573496359142-b8d87734a5a2?w=300",
    "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1509358271058-acd22cc93898?w=1200&q=80",
    "readTime": "5 min read",
    "excerpt": "Period cycle ke alag-alag dino me alag beej khane se estrogen aur progesterone balance hota hai. Iska bilkul aasan homemade tarika.",
    "content": "<p>Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) and irregular menstrual cycles affect more than 1 in 5 young Indian women today. While medical management is essential, daily dietary habits play an immense role in modulating androgen production and supporting cellular insulin sensitivity.</p>\n<h2>Why Label Transparency Matters Here</h2>\n<p>Seed cycling has emerged as a gentle, whole-food nutritional habit. However, commercial 'seed cycling powders' sold online are often heavily marked up, pre-ground months in advance (causing delicate omega-3 oils to oxidize and turn rancid), and filled with artificial flavors or stevia extracts that irritate sensitive gut microbiomes.</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>GudTree Golden Rule:</strong> Freshness is critical. Buy whole, raw seeds, roast them gently on low flame to preserve lignans, and consume them as a crunchy evening tea accompaniment.</p></blockquote>\n<h2>Smart Daily Swaps for Clean Eating</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Phase 1: Follicular Phase (Day 1 to 14):</strong> Consume 1 tablespoon each of raw pumpkin seeds (rich in zinc for follicle growth) and freshly roasted flaxseeds (rich in lignans that bind excess estrogen).</li>\n  <li><strong>Phase 2: Luteal Phase (Day 15 to 28):</strong> Switch to 1 tablespoon each of raw sunflower seeds (rich in selenium and vitamin E) and roasted sesame seeds (rich in calcium and natural lignans supporting progesterone).</li>\n  <li><strong>The 4 PM Hormone Crunch:</strong> Instead of chewing on bakery biscuits, toss your daily seed ratio with a pinch of rock salt and amchur for an energizing savory snack.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Quick Nutrition Audit Summary</h2>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Menstrual Phase</th><th>Recommended Seeds</th><th>Key Micronutrients</th><th>Hormonal Benefit</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>Days 1–14 (Follicular)</td><td>Flaxseeds + Pumpkin Seeds</td><td>Lignans, Zinc, ALA Omega-3</td><td>Supports healthy estrogen clearance &amp; ovulation</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Days 15–28 (Luteal)</td><td>Sunflower + Sesame Seeds</td><td>Vitamin E, Selenium, Calcium</td><td>Supports natural progesterone &amp; eases PMS cramps</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Pairing fresh, home-roasted seeds with clean hydration supports regular hormonal rhythms without relying on expensive, heavily processed commercial supplement packs.</p>",
