    "excerpt": "Subah oats ya meethi chai lene se 11 baje craving badh jaati hai. Besan chilla ya paneer bhurji lene se din bhar sugar stable rehti hai.",
    "content": "<p>Women diagnosed with PCOS or PCOD are frequently told to 'cut carbs and lose weight'. Seeking healthier snacks, many purchase packaged 'Diet Mixture', 'Roasted Quinoa Puffs', or 'Baked Corn Crisps' from local supermarkets, only to find themselves battling uncontrollable sweet cravings two hours later.</p>\n<h2>Why Label Transparency Matters Here</h2>\n<p>In women with PCOS, ovaries are hyper-sensitized to insulin. When blood glucose spikes rapidly, the pancreas pumps out high levels of insulin, which directly stimulates ovarian theca cells to produce testosterone and androgens. This hormonal cascade triggers adult cystic acne along the jawline, hirsutism, and persistent central adiposity. Many commercial 'diet' namkeens contain maltodextrin—a corn-derived additive with a glycemic index of 110 (higher than table sugar!).</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>GudTree Golden Rule:</strong> In PCOS, the glycemic index of your snack matters far more than whether it is roasted or baked. Maltodextrin in a baked snack triggers worse androgen spikes than traditional whole-food fats.</p></blockquote>\n<h2>Smart Daily Swaps for Clean Eating</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Check the Ingredients for '-dextrin':</strong> Reject savory snacks listing maltodextrin, dextrose, or corn syrup solids.</li>\n  <li><strong>Lead with Protein &amp; Healthy Fats:</strong> Roasted edamame, paneer tikka cubes, or roasted almonds buffer carbohydrate absorption and keep insulin flat.</li>\n  <li><strong>Savory Over Sweet for 4 PM:</strong> Avoid afternoon granola bars; switch to roasted kala chana with chaat masala and chopped cucumber.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Quick Nutrition Audit Summary</h2>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Snack Option</th><th>Primary Carbohydrate</th><th>Glycemic Index (GI)</th><th>Ovarian Androgen Impact</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>Market 'Diet' Namkeen</td><td>Corn Grits + Maltodextrin</td><td>GI &gt; 95 (Extreme Spike)</td><td>Stimulates testosterone release &amp; craving loops</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>GudTree Spiced Roasted Chana</td><td>Whole Bengal Gram</td><td>GI ≈ 28 (Slow &amp; Flat)</td><td>Maintains insulin stability, eliminates cravings</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Raw Almonds &amp; Walnuts</td><td>Dietary Fiber &amp; Plant Fats</td><td>GI &lt; 15 (Negligible)</td><td>Protects lipid profile, supports anti-inflammation</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Choosing whole, unrefined legumes and nuts over industrially modified 'diet' cereals helps break the cycle of insulin spikes and evening craving crashes.</p>",
