    "excerpt": "Protein bar khane se pet me gas aur dast kyu lagte hain? Maltitol aur chemical fiber syrup ke side effects jo brands nahi batate.",
    "content": "<p>Gym-goers, college athletes, and busy corporate workers frequently grab packaged protein bars as an on-the-go meal replacement. With prominent labels screaming '20g Protein', 'Zero Added Sugar', and 'Keto Friendly', these shiny bars command premium prices ranging from ₹120 to ₹220 per wrapper.</p>\n<h2>Why Label Transparency Matters Here</h2>\n<p>An audit of top-selling protein bars on Amazon India and Blinkit reveals that over 80% use maltitol syrup, sorbitol, or isomalto-oligosaccharide (IMO) as their #1 ingredient binder. Maltitol causes significant gas, abdominal cramping, and explosive osmotic diarrhea in sensitive individuals. Furthermore, instead of high-grade whey or authentic whole nuts, the protein comes primarily from cheap soy protein isolate (which contains high concentrations of phytates and is often poorly digested).</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>GudTree Golden Rule:</strong> If a protein bar contains more sugar alcohols and syrup binders than actual whole food ingredients, it is an ultra-processed confection masquerading as sports nutrition.</p></blockquote>\n<h2>Smart Daily Swaps for Clean Eating</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Check the Primary Protein Source:</strong> Whey protein concentrate or isolate, or pea/brown rice protein, is superior to generic 'soy protein isolate'.</li>\n  <li><strong>Beware of Maltitol:</strong> Check the Polyols / Sugar Alcohols row on the nutritional table. If it lists 15g+ of polyols, expect digestive discomfort.</li>\n  <li><strong>Desi Whole Food Protein Swap:</strong> A simple bag of roasted black chana (₹20) paired with a handful of raw almonds provides 16g of clean, bioavailable protein with zero gas or artificial sweeteners.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Quick Nutrition Audit Summary</h2>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Product Checked</th><th>Primary Binder</th><th>Primary Protein Source</th><th>Digestive Side Effects</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>Market 'Zero Sugar' 20g Protein Bar</td><td>Maltitol Syrup &amp; IMO</td><td>Soy Protein Isolate</td><td>Bloating, gas, sudden laxative effect</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Clean 3-Ingredient Date-Nut Bar</td><td>Pitted Whole Dates</td><td>Raw Almonds &amp; Whey Concentrate</td><td>Smooth digestion, natural fiber release</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>GudTree Bhuna Chana + Almond Mix</td><td>None (Dry Roasted)</td><td>Whole Bengal Gram &amp; Almonds</td><td>100% Clean gut tolerance, sustained energy</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Understanding protein quality and binder ingredients ensures your post-workout snack builds lean muscle without wrecking your digestive tract.</p>",
