    "content": "<p>For college students living in hostel dorms or freshers sharing rental PGs in tech hubs, hitting the recommended 1g to 1.5g of protein per kilogram of body weight feels financially and logistically out of reach. Mess food is notoriously low in protein (watery dal and carb-loaded rice), and expensive protein supplements are out of budget.</p>\n<h2>Why Label Transparency Matters Here</h2>\n<p>The fitness industry convinces young people that protein only exists in branded tubs or expensive imported meats. In reality, traditional Indian legumes, seeds, and dairy offer some of the most cost-effective protein sources on earth when paired smartly to balance limiting amino acids.</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>GudTree Golden Rule:</strong> Combining roasted Bengal gram (chana) with roasted peanuts creates a complete amino acid profile that costs less than ₹20 for 15g of bioavailable protein.</p></blockquote>\n<h2>Smart Daily Swaps for Clean Eating</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>The ₹25 Power Combo (22g Protein):</strong> 60g roasted black chana (₹12) + 30g roasted peanuts (₹8) + 1 glass cold water with a pinch of rock salt. Zero cooking, zero mess.</li>\n  <li><strong>The ₹35 Sattu Churn (20g Protein):</strong> 60g pure chana sattu (₹22) stirred into 300ml water with roasted cumin powder, black salt, and lemon juice.</li>\n  <li><strong>The PG Curd &amp; Seed Bowl (18g Protein):</strong> One 200g pouch of fresh plain set curd (₹20) topped with 20g pumpkin and sunflower seeds (₹15).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Quick Nutrition Audit Summary</h2>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Protein Source</th><th>Cost Per 25g Protein</th><th>Hostel Feasibility</th><th>Additives &amp; Preservatives</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>Imported Whey Isolate Scoop</td><td>₹120 – ₹170</td><td>Needs Shaker + Clean Water</td><td>Sucralose, Emulsifiers, Flavourings</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Hostel Bhuna Chana + Peanuts Mix</td><td>₹32 – ₹38</td><td>100% Ready to Eat (Store in jar)</td><td>Zero Additives (100% Whole Food)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Desi Chana Sattu Drink (70g)</td><td>₹25 – ₹30</td><td>Mix with spoon in any glass</td><td>Zero Additives (100% Whole Food)</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Consistency in meeting daily protein targets comes down to finding affordable, accessible pantry staples you can sustain every single day without financial strain.</p>",
