    "content": "<p>Peanut butter is an essential staple in almost every Indian fitness enthusiast's kitchen. It is praised for its rich monounsaturated fats, natural vitamin E, and plant-based protein. However, a significant portion of peanut butters sold in Indian supermarkets and on Amazon are heavily adulterated.</p>\n<h2>Why Label Transparency Matters Here</h2>\n<p>Natural peanut butter has one physical characteristic that mass-market commercial brands dislike: oil separation. When whole roasted peanuts are ground, natural peanut oil separates and floats to the top. To create an unnaturally smooth, shelf-stable paste that never separates, manufacturers add 'Hydrogenated Vegetable Oil' (often hydrogenated palm oil or cottonseed oil) alongside white sugar and emulsifiers.</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>GudTree Golden Rule:</strong> Oil separation is proof of purity! If your peanut butter has a layer of clear oil on top that requires stirring, that is a 100% pure product. If it stays perfectly solid at room temperature for 12 months, it contains hydrogenated vegetable oils.</p></blockquote>\n<h2>Smart Daily Swaps for Clean Eating</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Read the Ingredients List:</strong> Look for jars that list exactly one ingredient: 'Roasted Peanuts 100%'.</li>\n  <li><strong>Say No to 'Stabilizers':</strong> Reject jars listing hydrogenated vegetable oil, mono- and diglycerides of fatty acids (INS 471), or added table sugar.</li>\n  <li><strong>Store Upside Down:</strong> To naturally redistribute oil without messy stirring, store your natural peanut butter jar upside down in your cupboard.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Quick Nutrition Audit Summary</h2>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Peanut Butter Type</th><th>Ingredients List</th><th>Presence of Trans / Saturated Fats</th><th>Natural Oil Separation</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>Commercial Mass-Market Brand</td><td>Roasted Peanuts, Sugar, Hydrogenated Palm Oil, Salt</td><td>High (Added hydrogenated industrial fat)</td><td>Never separates (Chemically bonded)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>100% Pure Natural Brand</td><td>Roasted Peanuts 100% (or + Pinch of Salt)</td><td>Only natural monounsaturated peanut fat</td><td>Separates naturally (Sign of clean food)</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Checking the back panel ensures your daily tablespoon of peanut butter genuinely fuels cardiovascular vitality and clean muscle recovery.</p>",
