    "readTime": "4 min read",
    "excerpt": "Diabetic log dukan se 'Sugar-Free' biscuit late hain, lekin usme maida aur maltodextrin hota hai jiska Glycemic Index normal chini se bhi jyada hai.",
    "content": "<p>Across Indian households managing diabetes or borderline HbA1c, a blue or green box of 'Sugar-Free' biscuits is ubiquitous on the tea table. Doctors and well-meaning relatives recommend them as safe treats, believing that the absence of white cane sugar makes them harmless.</p>\n<h2>Why Label Transparency Matters Here</h2>\n<p>When you wear a Continuous Glucose Monitor (CGM) and consume two 'sugar-free' biscuits, the sensor reveals a sharp glucose spike reaching 160 to 180 mg/dL within 35 minutes. Why? Because while the brand omitted cane sugar, the base ingredient remains 65% refined wheat flour (maida) or high-glycemic starches. During digestion, salivary amylase breaks down refined starch into pure glucose within seconds of chewing.</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>GudTree Golden Rule:</strong> The body does not differentiate between sugar from a sugar bowl and sugar from digested refined flour. Refined maida spikes blood sugar with the exact same velocity as white table sugar.</p></blockquote>\n<h2>Smart Daily Swaps for Clean Eating</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Check the Total Carbohydrate Row:</strong> Even if 'Sugar' reads 0g, check 'Carbohydrates'. A single biscuit often contains 14g to 18g of fast-acting refined carbs.</li>\n  <li><strong>Swap for Whole Roasted Kala Chana:</strong> Unpeeled black chickpeas have a glycemic index of 28, producing a completely flat, harmless glucose response.</li>\n  <li><strong>Stone-Ground Methi Khakhra:</strong> 100% whole wheat combined with bitter fenugreek (methi) leaves, which contain trigonelline that enhances insulin sensitivity.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Quick Nutrition Audit Summary</h2>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Tea Companion</th><th>Primary Flour</th><th>Glycemic Index</th><th>CGM Glucose Spike Peak</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>Market 'Sugar-Free' Biscuit</td><td>Refined Wheat Flour (Maida)</td><td>GI ≈ 75 – 80</td><td>Spikes &gt; 165 mg/dL within 35 mins</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>GudTree Dry Roasted Makhana</td><td>Whole Puffed Foxnut</td><td>GI ≈ 45 – 50</td><td>Gentle rise, peak under 125 mg/dL</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>GudTree Roasted Kala Chana</td><td>Whole Bengal Gram</td><td>GI ≈ 28</td><td>Completely flat baseline curve</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Relying on whole-food legumes and seeds rather than industrially engineered 'sugar-free' baked goods protects your pancreas from chronic insulin strain.</p>",
